---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const APP = "https://login.ollastack.com";

const sections = [
  { id: "orgs", title: "Organizations" },
  { id: "roles", title: "Roles" },
  { id: "invite", title: "Invite teammates" },
  { id: "viewer", title: "The viewer role" },
  { id: "transfer", title: "Transfer ownership" },
];
---

<Base current="docs" title="Docs — Teams & roles — Ollastack">
  <div class="docs-shell container-wide">
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="side-eyebrow mono">/ docs / teams</div>
      <nav>
        <ul>
          {sections.map((s) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>
      <div class="side-back"><a href="/docs">← Back to docs</a></div>
    </aside>

    <article class="content">
      <span class="chip mono"><span class="dot"></span>teams &amp; roles</span>
      <h1 class="display">Share a workspace, not a password.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Group your forms and mailboxes into an organization, invite teammates by
        email, and give each one exactly the access they need — from full admin
        down to read-only.
      </p>

      <h2 id="orgs">Organizations</h2>
      <p>
        An <strong>organization</strong> owns content — forms, agent mailboxes,
        <a href="/docs/projects">projects</a>, submissions. Every member of an org
        can reach that org's content (subject to their role); nothing is shared by
        copying a token around. Manage your orgs at
        <a href={`${APP}/dashboard/orgs`}>Dashboard → Organizations</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="roles">Roles</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>role</th><th>can</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>owner</strong></td><td>Everything, plus org settings, billing, transfer/delete. One per org.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>admin</strong></td><td>Manage the team (invite / change role / remove) and edit org settings. Can't delete the org.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>member</strong></td><td>Full read + write on the org's content (forms, mailboxes, submissions, rules, projects). No team or settings management.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>viewer</strong></td><td>Read-only. See everything; change nothing.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="invite">Invite teammates</h2>
      <p>
        On the <strong>Team</strong> panel (admin+), enter an email and a role.
        We email an accept link; the invite also shows in the pending list. The
        invitee must sign in with that email to accept.
      </p>
      <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="k">curl</span> -X POST {APP}/api/orgs/<span class="hl">&lt;orgId&gt;</span>/members \
     -H <span class="s">"Cookie: ollastack_session=…"</span> -H <span class="s">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> \
     -d <span class="s">'&#123; "email": "teammate@acme.com", "role": "member" &#125;'</span></pre>
      <p>Roles you can invite: <code>viewer</code>, <code>member</code>, <code>admin</code>.</p>

      <h2 id="viewer">The viewer role</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>viewer</strong> is read-only across the whole workspace — perfect
        for a client, a stakeholder, or an on-call responder who should see leads
        and mail but never change anything. They can open every form, submission,
        and mailbox, but:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Write controls are hidden or disabled in the UI, with a "view-only access" banner.</li>
        <li>The API rejects every mutation (create / edit / delete / send / clear) with a not-found or forbidden response — enforced server-side, not just in the UI.</li>
        <li>They can't create content, manage the team, or touch org settings.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Promote a viewer to <code>member</code> any time to unlock writes.</p>

      <h2 id="transfer">Transfer ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The owner can hand the org to another member (owner-only). The new owner
        takes over; the previous owner stays on as an admin so they keep access.
      </p>
      <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="k">curl</span> -X POST {APP}/api/orgs/<span class="hl">&lt;orgId&gt;</span>/transfer-ownership \
     -H <span class="s">"Cookie: ollastack_session=…"</span> -H <span class="s">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> \
     -d <span class="s">'&#123; "userId": "&lt;newOwnerUserId&gt;" &#125;'</span></pre>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={`${APP}/dashboard/orgs`}>Manage your team</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/docs">Back to docs</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .docs-shell { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; gap: 56px; padding: 64px 28px 96px; }
  .sidebar { position: sticky; top: 80px; align-self: start; }
  .side-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .sidebar nav ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
  .sidebar nav a { display: block; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .sidebar nav a:hover { background: var(--bg-sunken); color: var(--ink); }
  .side-back { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 13px; }
  .side-back a { color: var(--muted); }
  .content { max-width: 760px; }
  .chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 3px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .chip .dot { width: 6px; height: 6px; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 50%; }
  .content h1 { font-size: 44px; margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.05; }
  .content h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 48px 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
  .content .lede { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 620px; }
  .content p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content ul { line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 22px; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content code { background: var(--bg-sunken); border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; }
  .content table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 14px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  .content th, .content td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 10px 12px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  .content th { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-weight: 500; }
  .code { background: var(--code-bg); color: var(--code-fg); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 22px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .code .prompt { color: var(--code-prompt); margin-right: 8px; }
  .code .k { color: var(--code-cmd); font-weight: 600; }
  .code .s { color: var(--code-str); }
  .code .hl { color: var(--accent); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 40px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .docs-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .sidebar { position: static; } }
</style>
